  { q: 'How is this different from watching career advice online?', a: 'Online content gives general information. A live session gives you a specific decision path, execution order, and accountability based on your real situation, constraints, and goals.' },
  { q: 'What if I have no idea what career I want?', a: 'That is a very common starting point. Not knowing is not a problem. We help you narrow options using practical assessments, strength mapping, and market-fit checks before you commit to a path.' },
  { q: 'How is this different from normal career counseling?', a: 'Most career counseling is generic, outdated, and one-time. Many providers push degree-first decisions without high-value skill building. We focus on practical direction, high-value skills, earlier financial freedom, and ongoing support when needed.' },
  { q: 'Is a college degree enough for a high income?', a: 'A degree can support eligibility. In most cases, stronger outcomes depend on high-value skills plus proof of work.' },
  { q: 'Can I realistically work toward early financial freedom?', a: 'Yes, through profile-fit skill stacking, market alignment, and consistent execution over time.' },
  { q: 'Do you guarantee a job?', a: 'No ethical provider can guarantee a job. We guarantee practical planning, better skill direction, and stronger competitiveness.' },
];

